{"title":"1975 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems from the <b>1975 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=United_States_of_America_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"United States of America Mathematical Olympiad\"> USAMO</a></b>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) Prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f35b4df2174c9e93d13d91ef893d3c1743e22e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[5x]+[5y]\\ge [3x+y]+[3y+x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"18\" />,</center>\n<p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0b108cc310eb0dbbd5e0f930cdba3d178ebc84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/280a218bdb8d795b8bd3810c97c5b15a6cac3b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[u]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb30d1824269c52d9fd8ede8897e54aab111b3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> (e.g., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6096210e09bfe83fe866eebcae8b65febbf1a331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\sqrt{2}]=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"22\" />).\n</p><p>(b) Using (a) or otherwise, prove that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adf3172b9cbf506283e6114ccb395d9c4901dcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(5m)!(5n)!}{m!n!(3m+n)!(3n+m)!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"194\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>is integral for all positive integral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8859dbfb7a9ec734e16f2a88fb5cf1104eb6a39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> denote four points in space and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and so on. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f26ad9653299114d0981a70d9a07a4c995c2bed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC^2+BD^2+AD^2+BC^2\\ge AB^2+CD^2.\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> denotes a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/1/9712b1563b6ef1e0d2423b4d12e37c3f87c038ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(k)=k/(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e3480f1aa48a86bd4d5d4f1610fa2c5dea01b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,\\ldots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />, determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5acd5b4248d21e2216f12640fc8e538efdc600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two given circles intersect in two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Show how to construct a segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and terminating on the two circles such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35c5be2f05b1084421f2e03948388f219c22d4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP\\cdot PB$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> is a maximum.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1ce46c52cfe092b52af621b5ca152165e1e7826.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(150); defaultpen(fontsize(7)); pair A=(0,0), B=(10,0), P=(4,0), Q=(3.7,-2.5); draw(A--B); draw(circumcircle(A,P,Q)); draw(circumcircle(B,P,Q)); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,(-1,1));label(&quot;P&quot;,P,(0,1.5));label(&quot;B&quot;,B,(1,1));label(&quot;Q&quot;,Q,(-0.5,-1.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A deck of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> playing cards, which contains three aces, is shuffled at random (it is assumed that all possible card distributions are equally likely). The cards are then turned up one by one from the top until the second ace appears. Prove that the expected (average) number of cards to be turned up is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/9751a9feb47425ab2a6a9843788db1b84e9df5d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO\" title=\"1975 USAMO\">1975 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_USAMO\" title=\"1974 USAMO\">1974 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO\" title=\"1976 USAMO\">1976 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195219\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 182/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4842/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.756      1 -total\n 56.92%    6.692      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 41.31%    4.857      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7554:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017195219 and revision id 53427. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}